"""Escaped non-ASCII bytes (layers.1.mlp.down_proj:2951).

The component reads text that spells out UTF-8 bytes as backslash escapes, as in the
literal string "\\xe2\\x80\\x99" (a curly apostrophe), or as HTML numeric entities such
as "&#39;". It fires on the hex digit that completes such an escape:

- the second digit of a \\xHH escape: strongest for continuation bytes (80-BF, the
  trailing bytes of a multi-byte character), weaker for lead bytes (C2-EF);
- the first digit of a \\xHH escape: moderate if it is 8 or 9 (a continuation byte);
- the bare "\\x" token: a small value;
- the second digit of a numeric entity like &#39;: strong; the first digit: weak.

Everywhere else it predicts 0. The program keeps only the last 12 characters of text as
its carry, so it runs in constant time per token.
