"""Component layers.1.mlp.down_proj:2976 -- a lexical "bi-word" detector.

What it does: this component is almost silent everywhere, and when it speaks it is
negative on a few specific words, all of them spelled with "bi":

- "bir" (Turkish "a / an / one"; also the tail of "hiçbir", "none"): strongly negative.
- "bis" (German "until"): strongly negative. The same letters inside English words
  ("bisector") barely register, so only the standalone word is counted.
- 必 (Chinese "must / necessarily"), the strongest trigger; its compounds 必要, 必须,
  必然, 必定 ... are weaker. 毕 (bì) is also strong.
- Cyrillic "бир" (the same Turkic word) and a few Latin "bi"-fragments (bit, bid, bib,
  bitter...) are weakly negative.

Everywhere else the prediction is 0. The program looks only at the current token, so it
needs no carry from earlier positions.
"""

READS = ()

BIR_WORDS = {"bir"}
BIS_WORDS = {"bis"}
BI_FRAGMENTS = {"bit", "bid", "bib", "bij", "bil", "abit", "ib", "itters", "itter", "bitter", "bitters"}


def step(carry, prefix, upstream):
    raw = prefix.token_strings[prefix.position].strip()
    word = raw.lower()
    if word in BIR_WORDS or (word.endswith("bir") and len(word) > 3):
        value = -4.0
    elif word in BIS_WORDS:
        value = -3.3
    elif raw == "必":
        value = -10.0
    elif raw == "毕":
        value = -3.7
    elif "必" in raw:
        value = -2.5
    elif word == "бир":
        value = -1.7
    elif word in BI_FRAGMENTS:
        value = -0.5
    else:
        value = 0.0
    return carry, float(value)

